{title: How Deep the Father's Love for Us (FJ_20_en)}
{song_number: 20}
{language: en}
{key: E}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[E]How deep the Father's love for [F#m]us, how [E/G#]vast be[A]yond all [E/G#]measure,
[C#m7]that He should give His only [F#m]Son to [E/G#]make a [A]wretch His [B]treasure.
[E/G#]How great the pain of searing [A/C#]loss; the [E/B]Father turns His face a[B]way,
[E/G#]as wounds which mar the Chosen [A]One bring [E/B]many sons to [E]glory.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[E]Behold the man upon a [F#m]cross, my [E/G#]sin up[C#m7]on His [B]shoulders;
[E]ashamed, I hear my mocking voice [F#m]call [E/G#]out a[A]mong the [B]scoffers.
[E/G#]It was my sin that held Him [A/C#]there un[E/B]til it was accom[B]plished;
[E/G#]His dying breath has brought me [A]life; I [E/B]know that it is [E]finished.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[E]I will not boast in any[F#m]thing: no [E/G#]gifts, no [C#m7]power, no [B]wisdom;
[E]but I will boast in Jesus Christ, [F#m]His [E/G#]death and [A]resur[B]rection.
[E/G#]Why should I gain from His re[A/C#]ward? I [E/B]cannot give an [B]answer,
[E/G#]but this I know with all my [A]heart: His [E/B]wounds have paid my [E]ransom.
{end_of_verse}
